1
00:00:00,170 --> 00:00:02,997
Dependabot opened this pull request on my demo shop.

2
00:00:02,997 --> 00:00:06,130
It bumps the React Query library from version 4 to 5.

3
00:00:06,130 --> 00:00:08,042
All three CI checks are green.

4
00:00:08,042 --> 00:00:11,230
This is what Kane CLI saw on that commit.

5
00:00:11,319 --> 00:00:12,999
CI checks that the code builds.

6
00:00:12,999 --> 00:00:14,439
It does not open the app.

7
00:00:14,439 --> 00:00:16,068
Bumpproof does.

8
00:00:16,068 --> 00:00:19,394
Bumpproof builds the base branch and the pull request in a

9
00:00:19,394 --> 00:00:20,580
Docker sandbox.

10
00:00:20,580 --> 00:00:25,001
Then Kane CLI drives a real Chrome through three journeys in

11
00:00:25,001 --> 00:00:29,128
plain English: browse, checkout, and the account page.

12
00:00:29,202 --> 00:00:31,090
This is the real run, sped up.

13
00:00:31,090 --> 00:00:33,730
Kane CLI has three jobs here: test the base,

14
00:00:33,730 --> 00:00:37,062
test the pull request, and later test the fix.

15
00:00:37,138 --> 00:00:39,245
On the base, all three journeys pass.

16
00:00:39,245 --> 00:00:41,138
On the pull request, all three fail.

17
00:00:41,138 --> 00:00:43,928
Kane says the Orders tab leads to a blank page.

18
00:00:43,928 --> 00:00:45,591
The browser console shows why:

19
00:00:45,591 --> 00:00:48,438
it cannot read "orders" of undefined.

20
00:00:48,522 --> 00:00:51,442
The verdict is written by code, not by a model.

21
00:00:51,442 --> 00:00:54,682
A journey that passes on the base and fails on the pull request

22
00:00:54,682 --> 00:00:56,302
is a regression.

23
00:00:56,380 --> 00:00:58,080
Then Claude Code gets the failure,

24
00:00:58,080 --> 00:01:00,113
the console error and the release notes.

25
00:01:00,113 --> 00:01:01,687
It has file tools only.

26
00:01:01,687 --> 00:01:02,967
No shell and no web.

27
00:01:02,967 --> 00:01:05,360
It may not change the bumped version.

28
00:01:05,439 --> 00:01:06,619
This is the real prompt.

29
00:01:06,619 --> 00:01:09,539
The lines that came from Kane are marked.

30
00:01:09,613 --> 00:01:10,973
It changes two lines.

31
00:01:10,973 --> 00:01:14,200
In version 5 the "loading" status is called "pending".

32
00:01:14,200 --> 00:01:17,153
It quotes that line from the upgrade guide.

33
00:01:17,236 --> 00:01:20,583
The fix is built again, and Kane runs every journey again.

34
00:01:20,583 --> 00:01:22,052
Three of three pass.

35
00:01:22,052 --> 00:01:25,416
Only then does Bumpproof accept the fix.

36
00:01:25,485 --> 00:01:28,317
It posts one comment on the pull request: the table,

37
00:01:28,317 --> 00:01:30,098
what Kane saw, and the patch.

38
00:01:30,098 --> 00:01:32,312
It pushes the fix to the bot's branch.

39
00:01:32,312 --> 00:01:33,765
It does not merge.

40
00:01:33,765 --> 00:01:35,825
A person decides.

41
00:01:35,903 --> 00:01:40,383
That run took 22 minutes and 102 Kane credits.

42
00:01:40,383 --> 00:01:43,603
The fix cost 18 cents.

43
00:01:43,682 --> 00:01:45,842
The second catch is pull request 3.

44
00:01:45,842 --> 00:01:49,042
It bumps React Router from version 6 to 7.

45
00:01:49,042 --> 00:01:50,112
CI is green.

46
00:01:50,112 --> 00:01:53,942
Nothing crashes, and the console shows no new error.

47
00:01:54,021 --> 00:01:57,561
On the account page, Kane CLI clicked Orders, then Overview.

48
00:01:57,561 --> 00:01:59,101
The Overview tab was marked,

49
00:01:59,101 --> 00:02:01,051
but the page still showed the orders.

50
00:02:01,051 --> 00:02:04,121
The text it was told to check never appeared.

51
00:02:04,203 --> 00:02:07,943
Claude Code traced it to a changed routing default in version 7

52
00:02:07,943 --> 00:02:09,403
and changed eight lines.

53
00:02:09,403 --> 00:02:12,383
Then Kane passed all three journeys again.

54
00:02:12,453 --> 00:02:15,304
In all, it ran on four Dependabot pull requests on this

55
00:02:15,304 --> 00:02:16,013
repository.

56
00:02:16,013 --> 00:02:16,926
One was safe.

57
00:02:16,926 --> 00:02:17,813
Three were fixed.

58
00:02:17,813 --> 00:02:19,933
The date-fns bump broke the build,

59
00:02:19,933 --> 00:02:23,033
and Claude Code fixed it in six lines.

60
00:02:23,106 --> 00:02:25,586
Then I ran it on other people's pull requests.

61
00:02:25,586 --> 00:02:27,506
14 repositories, read only.

62
00:02:27,506 --> 00:02:29,106
8 could run in the sandbox.

63
00:02:29,106 --> 00:02:30,066
7 were safe.

64
00:02:30,066 --> 00:02:33,046
1 broke the build, and the fixer did not fix it.

65
00:02:33,131 --> 00:02:36,731
To test for false alarms, I ran each base against itself.

66
00:02:36,731 --> 00:02:38,991
8 of 8 came back the same.

67
00:02:39,082 --> 00:02:43,082
In the census, no pull request had green CI and a broken app:

68
00:02:43,082 --> 00:02:43,962
0 of 8.

69
00:02:43,962 --> 00:02:47,662
Both catches in this video are on my own demo shop.

70
00:02:47,749 --> 00:02:49,269
Limits: npm only.

71
00:02:49,269 --> 00:02:52,149
Apps that need a database or secrets cannot run.

72
00:02:52,149 --> 00:02:56,169
A failing journey costs many times the credits of a passing one.

73
00:02:56,260 --> 00:02:59,480
Everything here comes from the run files in the repository.

74
00:02:59,480 --> 00:03:02,280
You can replay any run without a key.

75
00:03:02,367 --> 00:03:06,007
Pull request number 3 is left unfixed on purpose.

76
00:03:06,007 --> 00:03:08,547
You can run Bumpproof on it yourself.

77
00:03:08,631 --> 00:03:09,559
Bumpproof.

78
00:03:09,559 --> 00:03:12,411
Open source, Apache 2.0.

